Both edits are in place and verified. Report:

## Files changed (2, CSS-only, additive)

**1. `ui/party/party.css`** — appended at file end (after `.party-shell a:focus-visible`, lines 359–367):

```css
/* W31 follow-up: on the rider filing header the link paragraphs share a line
   when both fit and wrap naturally otherwise. The driver filing keeps its
   wrapping flex header; the status and account pages do not match. */
.party-header:has(+ #form-steps:not([data-filed-by])) > p:has(> a) {
  display: inline-flex;
  vertical-align: top;
  max-width: 100%;
  margin-right: 0.5rem;
}
```

Selector matches the test constant `RIDER_NAV` byte-for-byte; carries all three required declarations (`display: inline-flex`, `max-width: 100%`, `vertical-align: top`). The rider-only scoping is correct: `index.html` has bare `#form-steps`, `driver-filing.html` has `data-filed-by="driver"` (excluded), status/account pages have no `#form-steps` sibling (excluded).

**2. `ui/styles.css`** — appended at file end, after the existing `@media (max-width: 760px)` block (lines 1616–1627):

```css
/* W31 follow-up: the console queue stacks to one column on narrow viewports;
   any inline open-failure stays a full-width row via its own grid span. */
@media (max-width: 1000px) {
  .queue-row {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  }

  .queue-open {
    justify-self: start;
    min-height: 44px;
  }
}
```

## Verification notes

- **Desktop pin intact:** base `.queue-row` at `ui/styles.css:1250` still holds the exact 6-column string `minmax(130px, 1fr) auto minmax(140px, 1fr) minmax(150px, 1.2fr) minmax(130px, 1fr) auto` — untouched, so the 1200px assertion passes.
- **Narrow widths:** new block covers 320/375/542/760/1000; `.queue-open` gets both `min-height: 44px` and `justify-self: start`.
- **No `overflow: hidden`** anywhere in either addition, matching the parent's exclusion expectations.
- No HTML, JS, tests, settings, memory or commits touched. No denied tools this round — Read and Edit were both available.

Awaiting the parent's full-suite and colour-ledger run.

