Both edits verified. Report:

## Exact diff — `ui/styles.css` only (2 hunks)

**Hunk 1 — `ui/styles.css:1294`** — one declaration added to the existing status rule:

```diff
 .queue-open-status {
+  flex: 1 0 100%;
   grid-column: 1 / -1;
   margin: 0;
   color: var(--red);
   font-size: 12px;
 }
```

`grid-column` retained (inert in flex, per brief); `role="status"`/`aria-live` markup, `:empty { display: none; }` and the error colour untouched.

**Hunk 2 — `ui/styles.css:1617–1640`** — the final follow-up comment + `@media (max-width: 1000px)` block replaced wholesale by four all-width rules:

```diff
-/* W31 follow-up: the console queue stacks to one column on narrow viewports;
-   any inline open-failure stays a full-width row via its own grid span. */
-@media (max-width: 1000px) {
-  .queue-row {
-    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
-  }
-
-  .queue-open {
-    justify-self: start;
-    min-height: 44px;
-  }
-}
+/* W31 follow-up: the queue row is a content-driven wrapping flex line at every
+   width — fields keep a readable basis and wrap as space runs out, the open
+   button never shrinks, and a populated inline status takes its own line. */
+.queue-list > .queue-row {
+  display: flex;
+  flex-wrap: wrap;
+}
+
+.queue-row > span {
+  flex: 1 1 140px;
+  min-width: 0;
+  max-width: 100%;
+}
+
+.queue-row > .queue-safety {
+  flex: 0 1 auto;
+  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
+}
+
+.queue-row > .queue-open {
+  flex: 0 0 auto;
+  min-height: 44px;
+  max-width: 100%;
+}
```

## Compliance against the brief and frozen contracts

- **Base grid untouched:** `.queue-row` at `ui/styles.css:1248` still has `display: grid` + the exact 6-column string; only the more-specific `.queue-list > .queue-row` overrides `display`, so gap/alignment/padding/border/colour survive.
- **Selector strings match the W15 exclusion set byte-for-byte** (`'.queue-list > .queue-row'`, `'.queue-row > span'`, `'.queue-row > .queue-safety'`, `'.queue-row > .queue-open'`; `.queue-open-status` already excluded) — digest stays stable.
- **Safety badge** inherits `min-width: 0` / `max-width: 100%` from the span rule while its own more-specific rule sets `flex: 0 1 auto`.
- **Test contract:** `display: flex` + `flex-wrap: wrap` at 320→1200; span `flex: 1 1 140px`; button `44px` / `0 0 auto` / `100%`; status `1 0 100%`.
- **No** breakpoint, transition, `overflow: hidden` or field reordering. Party CSS, JS, HTML and labels untouched — this round edited `ui/styles.css` and nothing else. No commits/push/settings. No denied tools.

Ready for the parent's regression run and geometry sweep.

