content.text:
All three edits verified by read-back. Report:

## Exact diff — 3 files, 3 hunks

**1. `ui/party/index.html:19`** — two adjacent nav paragraphs collapsed to one shared paragraph:

```diff
-      <p><a href="./status.html">Check the status of a dispute</a></p>
-      <p><a href="./driver-filing.html">Filing as a driver?</a></p>
+      <p class="party-nav"><a href="./status.html">Check the status of a dispute</a> · <a href="./driver-filing.html">Filing as a driver?</a></p>
```

Both anchors and destinations byte-identical; ` · ` inserted between them. No other bytes in the file changed.

**2. `ui/party/driver-filing.html:21`** — class attribute added only:

```diff
-      <p><a href="./status.html#reference-input">Look up your reference number</a> · <a href="./index.html">Go to rider help</a> · <a href="./driver.html">View the driver demo account</a></p>
+      <p class="party-nav"><a href="./status.html#reference-input">Look up your reference number</a> · <a href="./index.html">Go to rider help</a> · <a href="./driver.html">View the driver demo account</a></p>
```

Three anchors, two dots, labels and hrefs untouched.

**3. `ui/party/party.css:359–371`** — final rider-specific rule + comment replaced by the two shared rules:

```diff
-/* W31 follow-up: on the rider filing header the link paragraphs share a line
-   when both fit and wrap naturally otherwise. The driver filing keeps its
-   wrapping flex header; the status and account pages do not match. */
-.party-header:has(+ #form-steps:not([data-filed-by])) > p:has(> a) {
-  display: inline-flex;
-  vertical-align: top;
-  max-width: 100%;
-  margin-right: 0.5rem;
-}
+/* W31 follow-up: both filing headers share one compact wrapped navigation
+   paragraph; the smaller text applies only to these filing links. */
+.party-header > .party-nav {
+  display: flex;
+  flex-wrap: wrap;
+  align-items: center;
+  gap: 0.5rem;
+  margin: 1rem 0;
+}
+
+.party-header > .party-nav a {
+  font-size: 0.9rem;
+}
```

## Contract checks

- **New nav tests satisfied:** `.party-header > .party-nav` → `flex` / `wrap` / `0.5rem` / `1rem 0` at 320/542/1200; `.party-nav a` → `0.9rem` with `min-height: 44px` still from `.party-shell a`; both HTML files yield exactly one `<p class="party-nav">` with 2+1 and 3+2 anchor/dot counts.
- **W15 digest neutral:** the old excluded rider selector is gone and the new pair `.party-header > .party-nav` / `.party-header > .party-nav a` matches the updated exclusion set exactly — `PARTY_UNRELATED` (`7e8a0a63…`) stays stable.
- **Driver rule intact:** the `:has(+ #form-steps[data-filed-by="driver"]) > p:last-child` flex rule and its pill/hover/focus rules (lines 291–325) are untouched; its higher specificity agrees with the new shared values (gap 0.5rem etc.), and `margin: 1rem 0` comes only from the new rule.
- **Scope held:** no smaller text leaks to status/account links (those pages have no `.party-nav`); no JS, console CSS, tests, settings, memory, commits or push. Colour ledger unaffected (no colour declarations added/removed).
- **No denied tools.**

Parent-owned items remaining: rebaseline the two `FROZEN` HTML hashes (after byte-diffing the non-nav content), then run the suite and geometry sweep.
